# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Local machine / agent workspace artifacts
.DS_Store
.claude/
.worktrees/

# Standalone library-crate lockfiles. Contract crates keep Cargo.lock
# tracked for reproducible WASM builds; verifier crates are locked
# through them. Prover crates are off-chain bench-only binaries — not
# release artefacts — so their lockfiles are not tracked either.
plonk/verifier/Cargo.lock
plonk/prover/Cargo.lock
pq/verifier/Cargo.lock
pq/prover/Cargo.lock

# Stray `out/` directories from manual `stellar contract build
# --out-dir out` runs. The bench scripts route their build output
# into `mktemp -d`, but interactive runs occasionally leave one of
# these alongside a contract crate.
**/out/

# Bench-gas outputs are regenerated on every run and uploaded as
# workflow artefacts (or pasted into the release body for the
# testnet flavor). Tracking them in-repo would just create churn.
scripts/bench-gas/results-*.jsonl
scripts/bench-gas/results-*.md

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
